The ETS residual ACF shows fewer significant spikes, but the histogram displays left skewness, and the Ljung–Box test similarly rejects the null hypothesis of residual independence (\(p &lt; 0.05\)). This remaining dependence may reflect unmodeled epidemiological factors or unusual epidemic years(2009, 2017, 2019).

Returns at Different Time Frequencies
Daily log returns are aggregated into weekly, monthly, quarterly, and yearly returns. Since log returns are additive over time, each aggregated return is calculated as the sum of the daily log returns within the corresponding period.


